              "numbering": "20.2",
              "text": "Vendor shall defend, indemnify, and hold harmless Customer and its Affiliates from and against any third-party claim, and all resulting damages, costs, and expenses, to the extent arising out of (a) an allegation that the Services or Deliverables infringe or misappropriate an intellectual property right; (b) Vendor's breach of Applicable Law; (c) unauthorized access to or disclosure of Customer Data caused by Vendor; or (d) Vendor's gross negligence or wilful misconduct. Customer shall give Vendor prompt written notice of the claim, Vendor shall control the defence, and Customer shall provide reasonable cooperation."
